==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhakə/|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gml|de}} {{term|hakke|lang=gml}}. Compare {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|hak|lang=de}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# [[heel]] (of the foot)
# the back of the [[shoe]], which is around the [[heel]] (but usually <u>not</u> the [[sole]], for which {{term|Absatz|lang=de}} is used)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l/de|Ferse}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|hacke|lang=gmh}}. Pertaining to {{term|hacken||to chop|lang=de}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# [[hoe]]

====Adverb====
{{de-adv}}

# {(context|slang|lang=de}}) very [[drunk]]
#: ''Ich bin so '''hacke''', Mann!''
#:: I’m so '''wasted''', man!

